{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_v4vaikmnrrqol6p7wfsdwdxjkmsjbof6dewyfkh5hmvkihioftlq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The Rust translation is in `translation/` and builds clean with `cargo build --release` (zero warnings).\n\n## Layout (mirrors the C)\n| C | Rust |\n|---|---|\n| `src/main.c` | `src/main.rs` — menu loop, all 12 commands |\n| `src/shape.c` + `include/shape.h` | `src/shape.rs` — the 10 singleton shapes |\n| `src/scene.c` + `include/scene.h` | `src/scene.rs` — scene create/add/remove/print/equals/save/load |\n| glibc `<stdio.h>` behaviour | `src/cio.rs` — the C I/O semantics the program depends on |\n\n## Fidelity details that needed care\n- **Shared stdin stream**: one byte cursor is shared by `fgets`, `scanf(\"%d\")` and `getchar()`, with a one-character pushback, so `fgets` stops at the newline while `scanf` skips whitespace across lines and the `while (getchar() != '\\n')` drains behave exactly as in C (including consuming the remainder of an over-long line, since `fgets` caps at 63/255 bytes).\n- **`%d` conversion**: verified against glibc — digits accumulate at `long` width, saturate to `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN`, then truncate to `int` (`\"99999999999999999999\"` → `-1`, `\"2147483648\"` → `-2147483648`), and matching failure vs. EOF is distinguished.\n- **Reproduced bug, not fixed**: at EOF the C `while (getchar() != '\\n')` loop never terminates. The Rust version also hangs there and, like C, never flushes its pending stdout buffer.\n- **Buffering**: stdout is emulated as glibc's fully-buffered 4096-byte block writer (writing directly to fd 1, bypassing Rust's line buffering), so even the partial output of a killed process is byte-identical; `stderr` messages (\"Error: Scene is full\", file-open errors) stay unbuffered.\n- **Byte-exact strings**: art rows and names are `Vec<u8>` and were mechanically extracted from `shape.c`; scene names/filenames are raw bytes, so non-UTF-8 input, embedded NULs (`strcspn`/`strlen` truncation) and `strncpy` 63-byte clipping all match.\n- **Pointers**: shapes are heap-allocated once and referred to by `&'static Shape`, so `shape_equals` is pointer identity and `%p` prints a real address (values are inherently run-dependent in C too).\n- Quirks kept: `fopen(\"dir\",\"r\")` succeeding then reading nothing (silent NULL scene), loading >50 shapes emitting repeated stderr errors, `shape_idx - 1` wrap, validation order, and `main` always exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\nI built the C original with gcc and ran a differential harness (stdout, stderr, exit status, and produced scene files compared; printed addresses mapped to first-appearance identity tokens): **810/810 inputs identical** — 66 hand-written edge cases (empty/EOF input, malformed scene files, CRLF, NULs, Latin-1 names, 63/64-byte name boundaries, count > 50, negative counts, directories as filenames, max scenes, 300-char lines, huge/signed numbers) plus 744 fuzzed sessions, including 22 cases where both binaries hang identically. The scratch build/test directory was removed; `c_src/` is untouched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":220,"cache_read_input_tokens":125942,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":220,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98073a6b-861e-4508-bd1d-8e26e0c3a0a1","uuid":"d549d50d-f5c1-4471-98fd-6fd0928a0295","timestamp":"2026-08-28T05:27:40.610Z"}
